  "final": "Both `get_document` and `list_documents` now filter by tenant, owner and `deleted_at IS NULL`. The public check and a new scope check both pass.\n\n**Changes**\n\n- **`src/repository.py`**\n  - `find(connection, tenant, owner, document_id)` runs `SELECT id, title, body ... WHERE id=? AND tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL` and returns `None` when no row matches.\n  - `listing(connection, tenant, owner)` applies the same tenant, owner and deletion filters and keeps `ORDER BY id`.\n  - All values go through `?` placeholders, so quotes in names are handled by the driver.\n  - Result shape is unchanged: only `id`, `title` and `body`, with no deletion metadata.\n- **`src/service.py`**: passes `tenant` and `owner` through to the repository. Previously they were ignored.\n- **`checks/access_scope.py`** (new): covers deleted, cross-tenant and cross-owner records, and an owner name containing a quote. It also checks that injection-style tenant and owner strings match nothing, that results contain only the three fields, and that list order is by id.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- `python3 checks/public.py` passes.\n- `python3 checks/access_scope.py` passes.\n\nI did not change `checks/public.py`. The `find` and `listing` signatures changed, but their only caller was `service.py`.",
